WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.310
<v Krista>In this video, we're talking about</v>

2
00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:02.990
how to find the multiples of a number,

3
00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:05.500
and we've been asked to find the first five multiples

4
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.100
of each of the numbers we've been given.

5
00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.060
The multiples of a number are just the numbers

6
00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:11.930
that can be divided evenly by the number we've been given.

7
00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:13.790
In other words, what I want to do to find the multiples

8
00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:15.870
of a number are multiply the given number,

9
00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:19.640
in this case, one, by one, by two,

10
00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:22.760
by three, by four, and by five

11
00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:25.340
because we've been asked to find the first five multiples.

12
00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:28.630
So I'm going to say one times one is equal to one,

13
00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.230
one times two is equal to two,

14
00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:31.970
one times three is equal to three,

15
00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:33.570
one times four is equal to four,

16
00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:35.560
and one times five is equal to five,

17
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:38.010
which tells me that one, two, three, four, and five,

18
00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:41.350
these results I got here, are multiples of the number one.

19
00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:42.560
And I know that that's true

20
00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:45.570
because I can divide all of these numbers evenly by one.

21
00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:47.730
So when I say one divided by one,

22
00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:49.810
I get one, which is a whole number answer.

23
00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:51.220
When I say two divided by one,

24
00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:53.210
I get two, which is a whole number answer.

25
00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:54.870
Three divided by one gives me three.

26
00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:56.470
Four divided by one gives me four.

27
00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:58.160
Five divided by one gives me five.

28
00:00:58.160 --> 00:00:59.540
I get whole number answers.

29
00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:02.210
So if I want to find the first five multiples of three,

30
00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:05.980
I just want to say three times one, three times two,

31
00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:10.980
three times three, three times four, and three times five,

32
00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:14.620
and the results I get are three, six,

33
00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:18.140
nine, 12, and 15.

34
00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:20.530
So three, six, nine, 12, and 15

35
00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.840
are the first five multiples of three,

36
00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:25.710
and the three, six, nine, 12, and 15

37
00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:27.870
will all divide evenly by three.

38
00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:30.610
In fact, I can say three divided by one is three,

39
00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:32.620
six divided by two is three,

40
00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:34.560
nine divided by three is three,

41
00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.220
12 divided by four is three,

42
00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:38.290
and 15 divided by five is three.

43
00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:40.630
Or I could say three divided by three gives me one,

44
00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:42.560
six divided by three gives me two,

45
00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:44.260
nine divided by three gives me three,

46
00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:46.010
12 divided by three gives me four,

47
00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:48.110
and 15 divided by three gives me five.

48
00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:50.770
So we're just looking for the multiples of that number.

49
00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:53.930
Same thing here, I can just say 12 times one is 12,

50
00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:56.100
12 times two is 24,

51
00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:58.120
12 times three is 36,

52
00:01:58.120 --> 00:01:59.720
12 times four is 48,

53
00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:01.800
and 12 times five is 60.

54
00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:04.140
So all of these are multiples of the number 12,

55
00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.130
and I could keep going on to infinity.

56
00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:10.050
I could say 12 times 100 is 1,200,

57
00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:12.860
and 1,200 is a multiple of 12.

58
00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:14.650
As long as I can take the multiple

59
00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:16.520
and divide it by the original number

60
00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:17.940
and get a whole number answer,

61
00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:20.860
I know that this number is a multiple of this number.

62
00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:22.710
So finding the first five multiples of 20,

63
00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:25.640
we say 20 times one is 20, times two is 40,

64
00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:30.470
times three is 60, times four is 80, times five is 100,

65
00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:32.783
and these are all multiples of 20.

